          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pathika is pathin, \"path, road\", with the suffix -ika (MW): one who is on the road (CDIAL 7745). Pathin is an inherited Indo-European word: MW compares Greek patos, \"path\", and Latin pōns, \"bridge\"."
            }
          ]
        },
